Port pg_cron v1.6.7 to PostgreSQL 19.

Three changes, none of them behavioural. Recorded as a patch rather than a
vendored fork so that what we changed stays legible, and so this file becomes
empty the day upstream supports PG19.

meta/postgres-manifest.md carried this as "not root-caused to a one-line fix"
and an unresolved risk against three subsystems. It is root-caused now:

1. Makefile: -std=c99 -> -std=gnu11.
   PG19's c.h implements StaticAssertExpr() with C11's `static_assert`.
   Under -std=c99 glibc does not define that macro, so the token became an
   implicit function declaration inside a struct and the compiler reported the
   confusing "expected specifier-qualifier-list before 'extern'" at every
   AllocSetContextCreate() call site. This was the error that looked like a
   header-ordering interaction with <assert.h>; it is really just a language
   level. gnu11 rather than c11 because Postgres headers use GNU extensions
   (`typeof`), which strict -std=c11 rejects.

2. src/pg_cron.c: include storage/fd.h for max_files_per_process.
   It used to arrive transitively; in PG19 it does not.

3. src/pg_cron.c: SIG_IGN -> PG_SIG_IGN.
   PG19's pqsigfunc is void (*)(int, const pg_signal_info *), so the plain
   libc SIG_IGN no longer type-checks. port.h defines PG_SIG_IGN for exactly
   this case.

Verified: builds clean under -Werror, and the extension schedules and executes
jobs against postgres:19beta3-bookworm (dev/tests/workflow/03-cron-tick.sql).

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index c139cac..9839881 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -12,9 +12,9 @@ REGRESS = pg_cron-test
 MODULE_big = $(EXTENSION)
 OBJS = $(patsubst %.c,%.o,$(wildcard src/*.c))
 ifeq ($(CC),gcc)
-    PG_CPPFLAGS = -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-uninitialized -Wno-implicit-fallthrough -Iinclude -I$(libpq_srcdir)
+    PG_CPPFLAGS = -std=gnu11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-uninitialized -Wno-implicit-fallthrough -Iinclude -I$(libpq_srcdir)
 else
-    PG_CPPFLAGS = -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-implicit-fallthrough -Iinclude -I$(libpq_srcdir)
+    PG_CPPFLAGS = -std=gnu11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-parameter -Wno-implicit-fallthrough -Iinclude -I$(libpq_srcdir)
 endif
 ifeq ($(shell uname -s),SunOS)
     PG_CPPFLAGS += -Wno-sign-compare -D__EXTENSIONS__
diff --git a/src/pg_cron.c b/src/pg_cron.c
index e202d14..a842bd7 100644
--- a/src/pg_cron.c
+++ b/src/pg_cron.c
@@ -69,6 +69,7 @@
 #include "libpq-fe.h"
 #include "libpq/pqmq.h"
